{
  "info": {
    "name": "AeroLink API",
    "_postman_id": "f1a8d7b9-aero-link-prod-suite-0001",
    "description": "End-to-end Postman collection for the AeroLink microservices platform.\n\nCovers every public endpoint exposed by the api-gateway: authentication, flight search, bookings, payments, baggage, check-in, passengers (profile + loyalty), notifications.\n\nWorks against either local docker-compose (use the AeroLink_Local environment) or the live AWS deployment (use the AeroLink_AWS environment).\n\n## How to use\n\n1. Import the collection and one of the two environments.\n2. Pick the environment in the top-right dropdown.\n3. Run `Auth \u2192 Login (passenger)` first \u2014 the test script auto-saves the JWT into the `accessToken` variable.\n4. All subsequent protected requests pick up the token automatically via collection-level Bearer auth.\n\nThe `Smoke / End-to-End Flow` folder runs an entire booking journey in order \u2014 use `Runner` (or Newman CLI) to execute it as one CI-style integration check.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Collection-level pre-request: nothing global. Per-request scripts handle their own setup."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Collection-level fallback test: every response should be JSON when 2xx, or text/json when error.",
          "pm.test('response has a body', function () { pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.not.be.empty; });"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8000",
      "description": "Set by the environment. http://localhost:8000 for local; https://d360csr5wvytoh.cloudfront.net for AWS."
    },
    {
      "key": "accessToken",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Populated by the Login request's test script."
    },
    {
